X server fix 1, S1: PolyFillRect honours the GC's raster op (build-tree patch
against isoriano1968/x11r6.3-amix cb61a21, applied after zz9000hw-modes.patch).

ZZ9000SolidRect wrote fgPixel whatever pGC->alu said, so a GXxor rubber
band (an outline move, XFillRectangle, a wide XDrawRectangle) drawn twice
stayed on screen instead of erasing itself.  Non-GXcopy fills now go through
miPolyFillRect, which reaches ZZ9000FillSpans; that one already implements
all sixteen raster ops.  The GXcopy fast path is unchanged.

Proof: x11/bench/xorfill (fill and wide FAIL on 709b8a97, the rig, 2026-09-27).

--- a/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/rtg/zz9000/zz9000draw.c
+++ b/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/rtg/zz9000/zz9000draw.c
@@ -370,7 +370,15 @@
 **
 ** Window drawables: direct framebuffer fill.
 ** Pixmap drawables: CPU fill (blitter addresses VRAM, not host memory).
+**
+** Only GXcopy is filled here; the loops below write fgPixel and cannot
+** apply a raster op.  Any other alu goes through miPolyFillRect, which
+** calls this GC's FillSpans (ZZ9000FillSpans implements all sixteen), so
+** a GXxor rubber band drawn twice erases itself instead of staying on
+** screen.
 */
+extern void miPolyFillRect();
+
 void
 ZZ9000SolidRect(pDraw, pGC, nrects, prects)
 DrawablePtr pDraw;
@@ -393,6 +401,12 @@
     int             cx1, cy1, cx2, cy2;
     int             y, w, h;
 
+    if (pGC->alu != GXcopy)
+    {
+        miPolyFillRect(pDraw, pGC, nrects, prects);
+        return;
+    }
+
     while (nrects--)
     {
         rx1 = xorg + (int) prects->x;
